& [RawDictation] is preserved without canonicalization
  + [text] is "so I'm feeling that we have a strong definition for the Scribe and Refiner faculties as patterns we've outlined in relation to Cantor behavior, but the identity and boundary functions of Honesty and Security are underdeveloped... and maybe this is a higher order of behavior? Honesty and Security need to detect boundaries and find natural relationships and identify when boundary is being crossed in an inauthentic way, and whether that boundary violation is in respect to shifting that boundary (deception) or ... I'm wondering how to describe ... can we define Honesty and Security issues as identity boundary issues? I have the impulse that is the true nature of violation of Honesty and Security, a kind of violation on the boundary or within the scope of identity, to rearrange attribution in such a way that weakens the framework of reasoning around the subject material, to make it subject to another domain by means that constitute de-centering of intention or purpose, a use case that has a wider scope of affect than intended purposes... in that are signals of deception and/or weakening of constraints."

& [ImmediateContext] preserves the active design pressure
  + Cantor now has a signed and implemented first-slice IdentityBoundary form with Honesty and Security as boundary guardians
  + current validation classifies static boundary domains but does not model boundary transition, attribution displacement, purpose displacement, constraint weakening, or effect-radius expansion
  + Weaver and Planner project relational and temporal combinatory potential inside guarded boundaries
  - never: treat this context as a canonical interpretation of the raw wording

& [UnresolvedTerms] remain deliberately open
  + [natural_relationship] may mean an evidence-supported typed relation whose existence does not merge identities or transfer properties automatically
  + [inauthentic_crossing] may mean concealed, unsupported, misattributed, unauthorized, or purpose-displacing boundary transition
  + [shifting_boundary] may be legitimate when explicit and governed or deceptive when hidden and falsely represented as preservation
  + [within_scope_violation] may mean erosion or rearrangement of constitutive identity even without crossing the outer boundary
  + [de_centering] may mean replacement of the declared subject or purpose by a wider or different governing domain
  + [wider_scope_of_affect] may mean unaccounted expansion in affected identities, resources, decisions, people, duration, or effects

